2:` segment, not a value's `version`, distinguishes a major cache generation. `schemaVersion` is payload/protocol shape (current `ImSnapshotV2Payload.SCHEMA_VERSION=1`); `versionDomain` is `WARMUP_V1` versus `BUSINESS_V1` data origin; `version` is same-object monotonic/CAS protection. Do not copy the stale `schemaVersion: 2` example from `docs/yopu-cloud-platform-缓存架构整改方案-V1.0.md`. [Task 3]\n- V2 templates must retain Redis runtime hash tags: `{{userId}}`/`{{groupId}}` become `{arg}` in `ImSnapshotV2Keys`, whereas V1 single-brace placeholders lose braces. Existing V1 upgrades use an independent `:v2:` Key plus dual write and Shadow comparison; new caches can start directly at V2. Register each Key in `RedisKeySpec` with Type/Codec/Schema, and never mix `StringCodec` and `JsonJacksonCodec` on one Key. Snapshot V2 needs same-tag formal/staging/manifest/fence; ordinary C2 caches do not need the full snapshot protocol. [Task 3]\n- For compatible additive payload changes, stay in the current key namespace and handle compatibility through `schemaVersion`; use `v2` → `v3` only for destructive changes. When retiring V1, explicitly clean the old namespace, manifest, and fence by domain to avoid `noeviction` capacity leakage. [Task 3]\n- Slow cache-invalidation Outbox consumption is intentional in this checkout: `CacheInvalidationOutboxProcessor` has `BATCH_SIZE=200`, `@Scheduled(fixedDelay=60_000)`, and oldest-first scanning, so 1577 PENDING needs at least eight cycles (about eight minutes plus work); ~8800 records need about 44 minutes under the same ceiling. Actual cycle time is processing plus the fixed 60-second delay. [Task 4]\n- Each item is serial `tryClaim` (`REQUIRES_NEW`) → MySQL fact read/Redis staging+formal/Lua RENAME/manifest/fence-CAS projection → `markCompleted` (`REQUIRES_NEW`), so DB/Redis round trips dominate. PENDING disappearing after claim means PROCESSING, not completed; retries use `min(60*2^N,3600)` and future `NEXT_RETRY_TIME` records are not scanned. `LEASE_DURATION_SECONDS=120`; acceptance remains `outbox_pending_oldest_seconds<120s` and `FAILED=0`. Safe semantic-preserving accelerators are larger batch, shorter delay, or more instances because `tryClaim` atomically prevents duplicate ownership. [Task 4]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Symptom: counters are empty on 233 although requests were made. Cause: sticky routing sent the user to 232. Fix: locate the node from gateway ACCESS logs and judge metric increments there (or collect both nodes). [Task 1]\n- Symptom: direct 232 SSH, Nacos 8848, or 232 actuator access times out. Fix: hop via 233, use Nacos 9000, and inspect actuator/env on 233 only. V2 sample keys without `{uid}`/`{gid}` will falsely appear absent. [Task 1]\n- PowerShell nested SSH/heredoc quoting breaks (`tail`/`registered` interpreted as commands); generate the remote call in a Python script rather than adding escaping layers. [Task 1]\n- PowerShell `rg -n -S \"...{{userId}}...\"` treats `{{` as a regex repetition and fails with `regex parse error: repetition operator missing expression`; for literal double-brace templates use `Select-String -Path <files> -Pattern 'pat1','pat2'`. A display-layer rendering of Outbox/Scheduled as `ln`/`n` is not source evidence; resolve the actual class names before reporting. [Task 3][Task 4]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / Redis Key domain inventory, task-board visualization, and IM-Account architecture documentation\nscope: Build source-backed Redis Key inventories using the required business-semantics/Type/Codec/Schema format; review against the codec contract, and deliver a visible all-domain board while preserving the source-vs-runtime boundary.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=key call sites and current checkout coverage are branch-specific; the inventory method, codec roots, visualization pattern, and runtime-SCAN boundary are reusable.\n\n## Task 1: Inventory, review, and corr