overed remote endpoints, and no shared-environment impact after shutdown. [Task 1]\n- The preferred durable solution is Android source with a `localDebug` flavor that changes `BuildConfig.BASE_URL` / `ApiConstants` / Retrofit creation. An APK-only route requires decode -> locate domain -> edit -> rebuild -> zipalign -> sign; re-signing cannot replace the original formal app and signature/anti-tamper, channel verification, hot update, login, push, or payment dependencies may fail. [Task 2]\n- In unpacked debug v2.10.6, `classes20.dex` `com/youpu/app/config/AppConfig` contains business gateway `http://10.168.1.233:9001/` and WebSocket `ws://10.168.1.233:9001/ws`; the `classes28.dex` `http://10.38.162.35:9085` belongs to an analytics/logging SDK, not the business gateway. Search efficiently with `rg -a -o --no-filename \"10\\\\.168\\\\.\\\\d{1,3}\\\\.\\\\d{1,3}\" <dir> | Sort-Object -Unique`, then inspect surrounding strings/classes. [Task 2]\n- Beta v2.10.7 is not runtime-switchable: `RetrofitManager$retrofit$2;->invoke` hardcodes `https://api.youpuzg.com/` and `ImWebSocketClient` hardcodes `wss://api.youpuzg.com/ws/`; apparent DEBUG/RELEASE/BETA enum code is overridden by `const-string`. Fastest route is the existing v2.10.6 debug package; HTTPS domain rewriting requires a trusted MITM certificate and an on-device pinning check. [Task 2]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Do not assume a named `AppConfig` class survives in a beta/release APK: v2.10.7 was obfuscated. When `rg` class-name search fails, locate URLs by scanning each DEX method's `const-string`/`const-string/jumbo` instructions and infer ownership from the containing class/method. [Task 2]\n- Symptom: `baksmali` URL returns 404 or local `jadx`/`apktool` is unavailable. Fix: install/use `androguard` (`python -m pip install androguard`); silence its logs with `logging.getLogger('androguard').setLevel(logging.CRITICAL)`. New `get_strings_analysis()` returns a dict, and xrefs may be incomplete, so direct bytecode scanning is more reliable. [Task 2]\n- Symptom: parallel analysis commands report `file used by another process`. Cause: shared stderr/log target. Fix: give each command a distinct log file. [Task 2]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM Redis snapshot Phase 2-4 authorization, dev acceptance, and contracts\nscope: Review and validate the one-domain-one-snapshot migration for IM user/group authorization, manifests, fences, Outbox, SHADOW cutover, Phase 3 dev dual writes, and Phase 4 contracts; product code/deployment remains separately authorized.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=source locations, current branches, dev/PRD topology, and rollout state are checkout/time-specific; codec consistency and fail-closed migration invariants are reusable.\n\n## Task 1: Inventory IM Redis snapshot omissions, codec boundaries, and Phase 0-5 compatibility\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-21T06-05-17-y5zE-im_redis_snapshot_refactor_omission_inventory.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\26\\rollout-2026-08-26T11-29-01-01a022ec-756e-7550-8c81-f92d7843c126_01a03c1d-30d1-7be3-979a-0958cee40032.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T05:39:09+00:00, thread_id=01a022ec-756e-7550-8c81-f92d7843c126, success: omission inventory and architecture document added; compatibility/checkpoint answers are explanatory, not run validation)\n\n### keywords\n\n- IM-Redis快照改造遗漏盘点-20260826.md, JsonJacksonCodec, StringCodec, InvalidTypeIdException, GROUP_STATS, FRIEND_VIEW, GROUP_MEMBER_VIEW, JetCache, deliver:*, RedisTemplate, SHADOW, legacy-write\n\n## Task 2: Phase 3 B6 dev group-four-domain V2 dual-write acceptance retest\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-25T10-46-51-ED4o-youpu_im_snapshot_phase3_dev_acceptance_and_phase4_contract.md (cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-