ext.getUserId()`, set cross-user shard with `TradeOrderUserShardContext` in try/finally, and expose only `GET /v1/trade/order/guard/location` publicly. Deployed dev proved start→list true→revoke→list false. [Task 1][Task 2]\n- A token is valid only when `guard:meta:{token}` exists, current HMAC verification passes, it is unrevoked, and it remains the order’s current mapping. Separate 51001 from 51004 and `200 + valid:false`, then match the share link’s environment to the environment that owns Redis; location reports refresh only `guard:loc`, never extend the 72h meta TTL. [Task 2]\n- `securityGuardEnabled` is recomputed by `batchIsActive(orderNos)` from Redis; revoke deletes the order mapping and list POST is not covered by the gateway’s GET cache. If an app still shows enabled after a confirmed revoke, capture the list response before debugging backend cache. [Task 2]\n- Query-rate increments must refresh the 60-second TTL every request. A no-TTL `guard:rlimit:q:{ip}` key accumulates permanently. `vicp.fun` does not pass a real client IP, so the tunnel shares the default 10/min/IP quota; use internal gateway IPs or redesign as IP+token / raise the test limit. [Task 2]\n- A newly created guard session must use its own `startedAt`; never return an old session’s timestamp merely because Redis/DB history remains. Verify `durationSec` on the deployed dev order, not only unit tests. [Task 3]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- `GuardTokenUtil` once checked for a 16-character signature even though it emits full 64-hex HMAC -> keep `SIG_HEX_LENGTH=64` aligned with token output and use constant-time comparison. [Task 1]\n- Adding a `GuardTokenServiceImpl` constructor dependency breaks direct unit-test construction -> update constructor calls and run module `test-compile` immediately. A deployed bug that persists may be a stale jar: GitLab deploy jobs are branch-gated, so verify job branch and deployed commit. [Task 1][Task 2]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform 