erge, dev-imtest, d7037b97bc77da196b47ef3130eaeda83a956575, JMeter, SingleChatPerformanceObserver, RBatch, AbortPolicy, MessageConsumer, offline queue, DLQ, async DB, CPU affinity\n\n## Task 10: Verify the post-refactor single-chat chain and assess 2000 QPS readiness\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-07T02-35-59-YZSP-im_single_chat_chain_and_2000_qps_capacity_analysis.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-08-07T10-35-59-019fda13-d193-7921-9f3a-bdc8ddee8b0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-07T03:16:13+00:00, thread_id=019fda13-d193-7921-9f3a-bdc8ddee8b0b, partial: chain verified; 2000 QPS not strictly accepted)\n\n### keywords\n\n- IMHandler, messageProcessor, SingleChatPersistenceTask, chatDbAsyncExecutor, saveSingleMessage, SingleChatSessionOutboxPublisher, SessionIndexPartitionDispatcher, CallerRunsPolicy, clientMsgId, 2000-QPS, SelectorManager\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user asked to rerun and first check whether the current pre message queue still has backlog -> inspect relevant RabbitMQ Push, ACK/offline, and business queues read-only; establish a clear baseline before applying load. [Task 3]\n- when the user required “用户数量可配置、M秒发送N条可配置” -> expose workload controls as JMeter `-J` properties, not fixed constants. [Task 1]\n- when the user required login, heartbeat, and business commands to be reported separately -> keep protocol accounting and business TPS separate. [Task 1]\n- when the user corrected the host roles: \"165 作为纯粹的压力机，47是IM服务器\" -> confirm host role and private address before attributing CPU, network, or JVM evidence. [Task 2]\n- when the user asked to analyze the bottleneck first and \"不要盲目加线程\" -> add segment evidence before changing pool sizes. [Task 2]\n- when load exceeds 500, the user specified \"165 as the primary pressure host, then 75, 89\" -> state host roles and split ownership explicitly rather than distributing users arbitrarily. [Task 4]\n- when the user asked \"修复，然后看看还存在啥问题\" -> after each repair, audit remaining reliability gaps and distinguish verified fixes from unverified risks. [Task 5]\n- when asking how the current 200-to-3000-user test differs from 0731 and \"how should I pressure-test next\" -> give the version/model differences, explicitly name non-comparable dimensions, then provide staged execution order, metrics, and stop conditions. [Task 7]\n- when optimizing IM performance, the user required latest analysis and real load-test evidence, and rejected treating final drain or historical cumulative metrics as a steady-business-window conclusion -> distinguish business-window deltas from drain state and static/code evidence. [Task 8]\n- when comparing branches, the user asked what is different and what can be learned for single chat -> separate production governance, load-test-only logic, and production-safe reusable changes; return a priority-ordered landing list rather than a diff dump. [Task 9]\n- when planning batch execution, the user explicitly said “优先调整批量执行并发，不增大队列” -> change only `executor-pool-size` through 8, 16, then only if needed 24/32; do not jump to 32. [Task 8]\n- when judging 2000 QPS, the user continued to require strict protocol closure and actual evidence rather than login success or sender statistics -> require `cmd5=cmd6=cmd27=cmd7=planned`, zero loss/duplicate/out-of-order, `ackPending=0`, and MQ/Outbox drain before making a capacity claim. [Task 10]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- Before a rerun, confirm the pre RabbitMQ backlog is cleared or record its baseline, then verify 47 health, the deployed JMeter file, and current process configuration. Historical backlog-induced `cmd=27` delay is not a capacity result for the new run. [Task 3]\n- `im_single_chat_duplex_continuous.jmx` uses one long-lived JDK 17 WebSocket per real user; users both send and receive, targets are mapped after login, and the final summary records cmd=5/6/27/7, QPS/TPS, P50/P95/P99, delivery/ACK rate, loss, duplicates, and ordering. `users.json` has only 500 valid users, so larger runs require more real credentials and friend mappings. [Task 1]\n- The validated cross-host P0 used 165=`139.196.23.165`/`172.20.196.192` as the JMeter pressure host and 47=`47.116.106.227`/`172.20.196.193` as the IM server. With two users at one message/user/second for 30 seconds, `cmd=5/6/27/7=60/60/60/60`, delivery/ACK were 100%, and loss/duplicates/out-of-order were zero: P0 only, not a capacity result. [Task 2]\n- `SingleChatPerformanceObserver` localized the gap to business execution through local Netty push write: cmd=6 P50/P95/P99=`489/504/748ms`, cmd=27=`449/459/663ms`, queued-to-executing is near zero, pushWritten is about 441–452ms, and pushWritten-to-ACK about 3–5ms. Add segmented timing across persistence, routing, MQ publish/confirm, MQ consumer, and push before altering fixed pool sizes; socket writes remain on the channel EventLoop. [Task 2]\n\n- For the 2000-user three-host run, shard 165=1200, 75=500, 89=300 without overlap and confirm each shard has local online-friend targets. `allLoginTimeoutMs` must exceed the login ramp; 240s ramp with a 180s gate timed out, while a 360s gate passed login. Capacity acceptance requires login, business, final protocol aggregate, and MQ/Outbox tail together. [Task 4]\n- The 2026-08-03 three-host result is not a capacity pass: `cmd5=60000`, `cmd6/cmd27=59998`, `cmd7=59786` (2 missing messages and 212 ACK gap); MQ/Outbox tail was not verified. The 165-only run also cannot support a strict 2000 msg/s claim because staggered login compressed send time (`cmd5=57172`, `cmd6/cmd27=57167`, `cmd7=57165`). Rework the JMX into a two-stage model with shared `businessStartAt` and a fixed 30s business window after all users log in. [Task 4]\n- `IMHandler.handleMessageDeliverAck()` had marked receipt without `MessageAckService.confirmAck(userId,msgId)`, leaving Redis pending keys and enabling duplicate direct pushes. The repair calls `confirmAck` for `cmd=7`; `IMServiceImpl` and `MessageConsumer` register pending before WebSocket write and cancel it on write failure; retry exhaustion/offline delivery uses idempotent `OfflineMessagePersistenceService.persist` before clearing pending/retry keys. `MessageAckService` defaults observed in source: pending TTL 300s, max retry 3, Redis-key scan retry. Package validation (`mvn -pl yopu-im/yopu-im-core -am package \"-Dmaven.test.skip=true\"`) and `git diff --check` passed. [Task 5]\n- The matrix script is `im_single_chat_duplex_continuous_codex.jmx`. A short-window result is acceptable only when login, business-send, final-summary, four-command closure, and MQ/Outbox tail all pass. `matrix-1500-rerun-20260803` met `1500/0` for main samples with MQ `ready/unack/consumers=0/0/8` and Outbox zero; retain the earlier 1000 login and 1500 business failures as variability/reliability evidence. [Task 6]\n- `matrix-2000-20260803` used 2000 threads, 240s ramp, 30s business window, and 330s duration after zero MQ/Outbox gates. Nineteen users did not reach a 180s login barrier; `IM_LOGIN_CONNECT 1981/0` was followed by `IM_BUSINESS_CONTINUOUS_SEND 1981/1981`. This is a load-generator/readiness failure, not a valid 2000-user IM-throughput result. [Task 6]\n- 0731 Go testing covered burst, group-chat, and mixed models as breadth reference; 0803 uses real-account, one persistent connection per user, bidirectional single-chat traffic, and `cmd5 -> cmd6 -> cmd27 -> cmd7` plus MQ/Outbox closure. Do not compare the two directly, and do not use user count as the sole capacity metric: at 1 msg/user/s, 2000 users also mean about 2000 msg/s plus connection/login load. [Task 7]\n- Before a 2000/3000 business run, establish login-only with a 240-300s ramp and login barrier at least 360s; then at the same connection count run low rate, 1 msg/user/s, and stepped rate. For each tier run a two-minute short steady phase and then at least ten-minute sustained phase, collecting protocol counts/TPS, P50/P95/P99, delivery/ACK, duplicate/order, MQ/Outbox, IM JVM/GC/CPU/threads/Hikari, and MySQL write latency/IOPS/slow SQL. [Task 7]\n- C0/C1 single-variable evidence identifies `TB_USER_SESSION_INDEX` UPSERT as the current 1000-QPS bottleneck: disabling it changed cmd6 P50/P95 from 17.9s/39.4s to 69ms/108ms, restored about 999.8/s persistence, and reduced lock waits 99.7%. P1-A batch-local merge/sort by `(USER_ID, SESSION_ID)` reduces one-batch contention but is not cross-consumer key serialization. [Task 8]\n- P1-A is not accepted: business P50/P95 was 40/56ms but Outbox unapplied was 96,146 (53%); same-key cross-batch/cross-consumer UPSERT contention remained. Use fixed-key partition serialization and bounded batching only after real P1-B load evidence. [Task 8]\n- Scheme B: `ChatDbBatchDispatcher` aggregates 50ms, groups `SHARD_UID % 32`, and defaults to an 8-thread per-shard executor; `ChatDbBatchProperties.enabled=false`. `ChatDbBatchPersistService` writes messages and matching Outbox in one transaction, retries only routing/deadlock errors, then uses row-wise idempotent fallback. Watch `[IM-CHATDB-BATCH]` and `[IM-THREADPOOL]`; pre-production 96/128-thread settings do not validate production 24/48 with `chat-db=false`. [Task 8]\n- `dev-im-merge` is a production candidate baseline (thread/MQ isolation, bounded queues, `AbortPolicy`, optional CPU affinity); `dev-imtest` is the stricter real-user JMeter/closed-loop observability system. Production-safe single-chat priorities are: `RBatch` for login/heartbeat while preserving routing/online/TTL semantics, move heartbeat Redis work off Netty workers and return explicit failure ACK on rejection, offline/DLQ fallback with `NACK(requeue=false)`, then minimize the persistence/session-index transaction. Async DB needs durable compensation and 500/1000-user A/B before enablement; CPU affinity/pool expansion are later experiments. [Task 9]\n- Verified chain: Netty decode/auth -> `messageProcessor` authorization precheck -> `SingleChatPersistenceTask` on `chatDbAsyncExecutor` / `im-asyncdb-` -> message main table plus session Outbox in the `saveSingleMessage` transaction -> local synchronous push or cross-node MQ (offline only when no online route) -> cmd6 ACK. The session index uses 16 serial partitions, 150 records/50ms aggregation, ledger deduplication, batch upsert, and post-commit cache invalidation. Source-default Outbox polling is 100ms but Nacos can override it at runtime. [Task 10]\n- The five-node 200 QPS x 120s run (23,994 messages) closed at aggregate 1000 QPS only; it cannot establish 2000 QPS or validate a high-single-host connection model. Use 1500 QPS x 180s for three all-zero rounds -> 2000 QPS x 180s -> 2000 QPS x 10min for three all-zero rounds, with `CallerRuns=0`, stable P99, and no sustained MySQL/Redis/MQ saturation. [Task 10]\n- Prioritize bounded queues with fast rejection/explicit busy metrics over `CallerRunsPolicy`, restore transactional persistent `(senderId, clientMsgId)` idempotency that returns the first `messageId`, then add segmented cmd6 metrics before tuning pools. Local synchronous push may reduce cmd27 but occupies `im-asyncdb-`; test the proposed independent bounded delivery executor with A/B evidence before claiming throughput gains. [Task 10]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Do not run directly when queue status, 47 health, JMeter artifact, or process configuration is unknown; do not attribute an old queue backlog to the new run's capacity. [Task 3]\n- `DuplexListener` cannot read outer JMeter `props`: `groovy.lang.MissingPropertyException: No such property: props for class: DuplexListener` -> pass command configuration through shared listener state. [Task 1]\n- A failed early smoke can be a script/runtime issue, not an IM performance result: inspect JTL `responseMessage` and `listenerError` first. For restarts, verify actual PID, 8084/8085, health, and `/actuator/beans` wiring for `singleChatPerformanceObserver`, not only the JAR filename. [Task 2]\n- `--spring.cloud.nacos.enabled=false` does not reliably suppress Nacos ConfigData import; a known recovery path explicitly supplies `--spring.config.import=optional:file:/opt/yopu-apps/conf/application-pre.yaml`, then verifies service health. Monitor RSS, Direct Memory, GC, and OOM before high-connection tests on 47 because `-Xmx50g + MaxDirectMemorySize=10g` leaves little headroom on 64G. [Task 2]\n- Do not call a run passed solely because all users logged in or a sender-side total looks complete. Require `cmd5 == cmd6 == cmd27 == cmd7 == planned`, zero loss/duplicate/out-of-order, `ackPending=0`, and MQ/Outbox tail completion. [Task 4]\n- Do not claim the new ACK/offline tests passed: existing `IMServiceImplTest.java:[119,33]` and `[121,34]` fail test compilation because `isRetryableShardingRouteException(IllegalStateException)` is missing. Remaining risks: offline-persistence failure retains only pending TTL, ACK misses are DEBUG-only, Redis full scans can cause retry bursts, and long JMeter runs do not reclaim `sent/byContent` maps. In PowerShell, quote whole Maven `-D` arguments. [Task 5]\n- When a 2000 run has incomplete login at the barrier, do not call the downstream business errors an IM capacity failure. Increase/parameterize `allLoginTimeoutMs` beyond ramp/readiness, ensure every login thread can reach the barrier, and collect target CPU/RSS/GC/EventLoop/connection and JMeter metrics before retrying. Do not begin 3000 until 2000 closes the full protocol and MQ/Outbox gates. [Task 6]\n- Stop escalation and return to the last passing tier if delivery is below 99.9%, the `cmd6 -> cmd27` gap grows, MQ/Outbox does not return to zero, P99 deteriorates, GC jitters, or MySQL stays saturated. Avoid unbounded `rg` over the repository; restrict it to report/JMX paths and bound output, since an 88MB result was truncated. [Task 7]\n- Do not equate MySQL global cumulative `Innodb_row_lock_waits` or `setAutoCommit -> socket read` with this run's row-lock cause: capture `BUSINESS_START/END` deltas and correlate `data_lock_waits`, `data_locks`, and `processlist`. `BUSINESS_END` and `DRAIN_END` are separate; final queue=0 is not a steady-window pass. [Task 8]\n- The new `SessionIndexPartitionDispatcher` initially appeared patched but its file was absent -> after adding files, run `Test-Path`/`Get-Item` before compiling. Its Maven package passed only with `-Dmaven.test.skip=true`; no P1-B load result exists. For a targeted reactor test, quote `\"-Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false\"`; a normal `-DskipTests` build was blocked by existing `IMServiceImplTest` missing-method compilation. [Task 8]\n- Static branch comparison is not a JMeter/service/capacity run. Long Chinese paths can make `git show` fail; prefer short paths, `git diff --stat`, class-name search, or the working-tree file. Do not promote virtual users, auth bypasses, or virtual group members into production paths. [Task 9]\n- Do not treat local synchronous push's lower cmd27 as a throughput gain: first measure its long-lived occupancy of `im-asyncdb-` and the full protocol closure. If high single-host connection tests show duplicate/ACK-pending noise on Java HttpClient `SelectorManager`, distribute load generators and repair the login ramp/barrier before attributing readiness failure to the IM server. [Task 10]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM message-quote protocol and acceptance design\nscope: Review and document the server-side message-quote contract, persistence, invalidation, and compatibility rules; this rollout did not implement business code.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=recheck ImCommandConstant, IMHandler, gateway contracts, and the approved document before implementation.\n\n## Task 1: Review and update the message-quote implementation/acceptance plan\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-30T07-11-07-7Fmu-im_message_quote_plan_review_and_protocol_update.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\30\\rollout-2026-07-30T15-11-07-019fb1dc-d31f-7872-b0b5-901078c5226e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-30T09:31:48+00:00, thread_id=019fb1dc-d31f-7872-b0b5-901078c5226e, success: design document reviewed and updated)\n\n### keywords\n\n- content + extra + mentions, extra.replyTo.messageId, /v1/im/message/quote/target, ImCommandConstant, IMHandler, cmd=5, cmd=6, cmd=11, cmd=12, cmd=22, cmd=27, QUOTE_MESSAGE_ID, QUOTE_STATUS, MESSAGE_EXTRA, outbox\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user asked “具体要提供几个接口给客户端” -> state the count of new client APIs, changed existing contracts, command matrix, and acceptance evidence directly. [Task 1]\n- when the user asked “补强后评审” and adopted `content + extra + mentions` -> expose blockers first, then make the user's protocol the contract and strengthen server validation/state consistency around it. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- The approved shape is `content + extra + mentions`: client uploads only `extra.replyTo.messageId`; server generates the quote snapshot/status/version and returns `extra.replyTo` consistently in ACK, push, and history. `extra` needs version, whitelist, and size validation; reject or strip unknown fields. `mentions` remains a separate executable-semantic field, with no @ business expansion this phase. [Task 1]\n- Protocol directions: single uplink `cmd=5`, ACK `cmd=6`; group uplink `cmd=11`, ACK/push `cmd=12`; single receive push `cmd=27`; revoke/quote invalidation `cmd=22`. String fast paths `handleSingleChat(String)` and `handleGroupChat(String)` must parse nested `extra.replyTo.messageId`; use DTO + `ObjectMapper`, not hand-written JSON. [Task 1]\n- Add one original-message-location HTTP API, `/v1/im/message/quote/target`; the other four are existing payload-contract changes, not five new APIs. Gateway `/v1/im/**` injects identity; never trust a client `userId`. Persist indexed `QUOTE_MESSAGE_ID`, `QUOTE_STATUS`, snapshot, and state version rather than scanning `MESSAGE_EXTRA`. [Task 1]\n- Revoke/cleanup is a separate cmd=22 `event` with `eventId`, `rootMessageId`, `stateVersion`, chunked affected quote IDs, `sequence`, and `lastChunk`; clients process idempotently. Keep hot-store updates atomic; use outbox/compensation for cold store and ES rather than promising a global transaction. Capability downgrade must cover WebSocket, HTTP history/offline pull, and device Push. [Task 1]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Do not confuse uplink, ACK, receive push, and revoke event; verify `ImCommandConstant.java` and `IMHandler` before writing the command matrix. [Task 1]\n- Do not mark all system messages non-quotable: freeze an allowlist by `msgType + content` subtype. Do not call design-document `git diff --check` success an implementation, DDL, Maven, or release verification. [Task 1]\n\n# Task Group: Windows screenshot OCR for model-usage/cost questions\nscope: Extract model-usage data from a supplied Windows screenshot; use when a Chinese “今天花了多少钱/今日模型用量” request provides an image but no account entrypoint. Do not turn ambiguous OCR output into a precise cost claim.\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents; reuse_rule=WinRT OCR availability and installed packages are machine-specific; the confidence and search-boundary safeguards are reusable.\n\n## Task 1: OCR a dark “今日模型用量” screenshot for DeepSeek cost\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-26T08-49-26-NN3F-windows_powershell_ocr_deepseek_usage_screenshot.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-08-26T16-49-26-01a03d42-8cbd-7d91-a7f8-ff810278023f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T09:05:58+00:00, thread_id=01a03d42-8cbd-7d91-a7f8-ff810278023f, partial: OCR method ran but no final cost/value was safely delivered)\n\n### keywords\n\n- deepseek, 今日模型用量, OCR, Windows.Media.Ocr, WinRT, PowerShell, TryCreateFromUserProfileLanguages, zh-Hans-CN, tesseract, cv2, control-chrome, mcp__node_repl__js, gray>150\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user attaches a dark screenshot and asks “deepseek今天花了多少钱” -> treat the screenshot as the primary data source; start with local OCR and use a logged-in platform only when available, rather than first asking for an account entrypoint. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- This machine has no tesseract/pytesseract/easyocr/paddleocr; Python 3.12 has PIL/cv2/numpy. The dependency-free option is `Windows.Media.Ocr` with `zh-Hans-CN`, after loading WinRT type projections and using generic `AsTask`/`Await`. [Task 1]\n- For a 185x225 dark image, `gray>150` and >4px row gaps separated the table header plus five rows. `control-chrome` needs `mcp__node_repl__js`; without that tool, a logged-in Chrome fallback is unavailable. [Task 1]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- `Unable to find type` and `Cannot index into a null array` mean the WinRT types or generic `AsTask` method were not loaded: call `Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Runtime.WindowsRuntime`, preload the required `[Windows...., ContentType=WindowsRuntime]` types, and filter reflection with `$_.IsGenericMethod`. Use `TryCreateFromUserProfileLanguages()` instead of an unloaded `Windows.Globalization.Language`. [Task 1]\n- Small dark-image numerals were inconsistent across OCR/enhancement attempts. If the number drives a cost decision, cross-check multiple enhancements and manually inspect, or get source/platform data; do not report a single OCR result as exact. Bound any `rg` search to likely app directories and a timeout—recursing through `D:\\soft`/AppData was slow and irrelevant. [Task 1]\n\n# Task Group: Windows Fiddler Classic and MEmu HTTP/WebSocket capture setup\nscope: Configure both local MEmu instances for Fiddler Classic HTTP/HTTPS capture, maintain reboot recovery, and distinguish direct IM WebSocket traffic from observed Fiddler frames.\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents; reuse_rule=local executable paths, ADB serials, certificates, UI state, and NAT/host routing are machine/session-specific; do not call WebSocket capture complete without a fresh `101 Switching Protocols` session and frames.\n\n## Task 1: Configure Fiddler Classic and MEmu proxy/HTTPS capture\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-29T01-44-35-GAwl-fiddler_memu_android_proxy_cert_capture_setup.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\29\\rollout-2026-07-29T09-44-35-019fab8b-84a0-7430-9ebe-eda54efd9ea5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T02:28:51+00:00, thread_id=019fab8b-84a0-7430-9ebe-eda54efd9ea5, success: Fiddler Classic on 8866 and both VM HTTP/HTTPS proxy paths verified)\n\n### keywords\n\n- Fiddler Classic, Fiddler Everywhere, MEmu, adb.exe, memuc.exe, 127.0.0.1:21503, 127.0.0.1:21513, 10.0.2.2:8866, 269953fb.0, AllowRemote, CaptureCONNECT\n\n## Task 2: Use a narrow host allowlist and reversible proxy on/off workflow\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-29T01-44-35-GAwl-fiddler_memu_android_proxy_cert_capture_setup.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\29\\rollout-2026-07-29T09-44-35-019fab8b-84a0-7430-9ebe-eda54efd9ea5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T02:28:51+00:00, thread_id=019fab8b-84a0-7430-9ebe-eda54efd9ea5, success: CustomRules allowlist and direct-connect recovery verified)\n\n### keywords\n\n- CustomRules.js, OnBeforeRequest, ui-hide, youpu, youpucq, youpuzg, 10.168.1.232, 10.168.1.233, settings delete global http_proxy, direct 200, Live Traffic, Inspectors, WebSocket, Messages\n\n## Task 3: Diagnose direct IM WebSocket bypass and restore HTTPS capture after emulator reboot\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-29T01-44-35-GAwl-fiddler_memu_android_proxy_cert_capture_setup.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\29\\rollout-2026-07-29T09-44-35-019fab8b-84a0-7430-9ebe-eda54efd9ea5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T02:28:51+00:00, thread_id=019fab8b-84a0-7430-9ebe-eda54efd9ea5, mixed: direct-connection diagnosis and certificate-loss repair confirmed; unread-count payload not extracted)\n\n### keywords\n\n- 10.0.2.2:12728, x-overridehost, 101 Switching Protocols, uni.UNI8C317FA.youpu, proxy:000, cert-missing, curl: (60), 269953fb.0, setup_cert_bindmount.sh, fix_fiddler_proxy.cmd, %%{http_code}, toybox nc -w\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when capture was too broad, the user said \"不要全部都抓，只抓ws和yopu相关的请求\", then added `10.168.1.232` and `.233` -> default to the narrow youpu/LAN allowlist and include every named host. [Task 2]\n- \"代理关了我的模拟器正常访问也得恢复\" -> proxy workflows must be reversible: verify direct access after disable and restore proxy, certificate, and 200 validation when re-enabling. [Task 2]\n- when asking to look in WebSocket for login unread counts, the user expects inspection of actual payloads, not a request to paste messages. [Task 3]\n- repeated \"代理又坏了\" / \"抓不到了\" after restarts -> run the one-click repair, report VM0/VM1 `200`, and point to the self-service script; a startup scheduled task was offered but not adopted. [Task 3]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- The final working capture tool is Fiddler Classic on `::8866`; check `Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 8866 -State Listen`. Its `HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Fiddler2` settings are `ListenPort`=0x22a2, `AllowRemote`=True, and `CaptureCONNECT`=True. MEmu ADB is `D:\\soft\\Microvirt\\MEmu\\adb.exe`; VM0=`127.0.0.1:21503`, VM1=`127.0.0.1:21513`, and host loopback is `10.0.2.2`. [Task 1]\n- Set each proxy with `adb -s <serial> shell settings put global http_proxy 10.0.2.2:8866`; use device curl through `-x 10.0.2.2:8866` and expect 200. `memuc.exe listvms` identifies index 0/1; install the CA with `setup_cert_bindmount.sh` at `/system/etc/security/cacerts/269953fb.0`. [Task 1]\n- Related skill: skills/memu-fiddler-proxy-repair/SKILL.md.\n- The Fiddler display filter is `C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents\\Fiddler2\\Scripts\\CustomRules.js` `OnBeforeRequest`: use `ui-hide` unless the host includes `youpu`, `youpucq`, `youpuzg`, `10.168.1.232`, or `10.168.1.233`. Restart/reload Fiddler after changes. Disable with `settings delete global http_proxy` and verify direct curl 200. [Task 2]\n- WebSocket frames, when routed through Fiddler, are in Live Traffic: select the `wss://`/`101` handshake, then `Inspectors → WebSocket → Messages`. The app's IM connection to `10.0.2.2:12728` bypassed the 8866 system proxy; no unread-count frame was captured. [Task 3]\n- Reboot restores MEmu `/system`, losing `/system/etc/security/cacerts/269953fb.0`: `proxy:000`, direct 200, `cert-missing`, and curl (60) mean rerun `setup_cert_bindmount.sh`, reset proxy, then expect proxy curl 200. `C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents\\fix_fiddler_proxy.cmd` is the canonical repair copy; a Desktop copy may be moved or renamed. [Task 3]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Do not recursively scan the whole disk for Fiddler logs/certs; start at `C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents\\Fiddler2` and `C:\\Users\\79873\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Fiddler`. `Fiddler Everywhere` winget downloads can hang; if needed, stop only the stuck winget and resume with `curl.exe -L --continue-at -` plus SHA256, but do not mistake it for the final working capture tool. [Task 1]\n- Mixed PowerShell/adb/shell quoting breaks `%{http_code}` and nested braces; wrap the remote command in double quotes from PowerShell. `toybox nc -z` is unsupported; use `echo | toybox nc -w 3 host port`. Keep `CustomRules.js` minimal: a compile error silently disables all rules. [Task 2][Task 3]\n- Do not claim WebSocket capture from a listener or long TCP connection: require fresh `101 Switching Protocols` plus frames. In the CMD repair script do not put `<-` in echo text because CMD treats `<` as redirection; invoke `cmd /c '...\\fix_fiddler_proxy.cmd'` without `< nul` from PowerShell. [Task 3]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IMServiceImpl benchmark bypass and Locust single-chat testing\nscope: Plan or implement a reproducible single-chat benchmark that retains the formal IM send path and MySQL persistence while suppressing Redis/Feign only within the controlled send branch.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=checkout-specific call-chain/line facts and partial design evidence; do not claim throughput, P99, or capacity until a real target-server run validates the counters and recipient delivery.\n\n## Task 1: Retain the formal IMHandler → IMServiceImpl send path for benchmarking\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-25T05-44-12-8wAs-imserviceimpl_locust_single_chat_benchmark_redesign.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\25\\rollout-2026-07-25T13-44-12-019f97cd-768a-7c03-9d9c-1b73fce49b04.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-25T08:55:16+00:00, thread_id=019f97cd-768a-7c03-9d9c-1b73fce49b04, partial: redesign/analysis completed; no target-server benchmark result)\n\n### keywords\n\n- IMHandler.handleSingleChat, IMServiceImpl.sendSingleMessage, BenchmarkMessagePath, Redis, Feign, MySQL, checkIdempotent, deliverMessageToUser, CallerRunsPolicy\n\n## Task 2: Evaluate and redesign Locust single-chat testing\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-25T05-44-12-8wAs-imserviceimpl_locust_single_chat_benchmark_redesign.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\25\\rollout-2026-07-25T13-44-12-019f97cd-768a-7c03-9d9c-1b73fce49b04.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-25T08:55:16+00:00, thread_id=019f97cd-768a-7c03-9d9c-1b73fce49b04, partial: current script assessed; strict end-to-end redesign remains pending)\n\n### keywords\n\n- Locust, locustfile_single.py, users_*.json, WebSocket, cmd=1, cmd=5, cmd=27, fixed-pairing, success=false, result-500.html\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when performance work begins, the user asked “先给出方案 md” -> inspect code facts and provide a reviewable plan before modifying business code or running a load test. [Task 1]\n- when the first benchmark bypassed the business service, the user corrected: “为什么不去 imserviceImpl 实现类中把第三方调用来源禁用掉呢” -> benchmark the formal `IMHandler → IMServiceImpl` send path; bare Netty/in-memory Channel is only a secondary baseline. [Task 1]\n- the user said “只要保证在发送消息的时候目前不走 Redis、不调 Feign 就行” and “落库保留” -> constrain bypasses to send-stage Redis/Feign; retain MySQL message persistence/conversation update and keep any no-DB run as a separately labelled baseline. [Task 1]\n- when the user said “我先测单聊” and asked how the script works -> start with standalone, reproducible single-chat Locust instructions and clearly distinguish the load-generator host from the target IM service. [Task 2]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- Formal single-chat entry: `IMHandler.handleSingleChat` → `IMServiceImpl.sendSingleMessage`; group entry: `handleGroupChat` → `sendGroupMessage`. The current send path also contains idempotency Redis, sender-profile cache, authorization through `RelationAuthorizationSnapshotReader` or `SendPrecheckFeignClient`, Redis routing/MQ/offline delivery, conversation cache, stranger limits, and moderation. [Task 1]\n- A valid persistence-retaining benchmark keeps message object/ID construction, MySQL or sharded write, and formal response; it bypasses only the controlled Redis/Feign/cache/authorization/routing/remote-MQ/offline-push/unread/conversation-cache/moderation side paths, with local online Channel delivery. Verify branch hit count, MySQL writes, local deliveries, and Redis/Feign/MQ/offline call counters all together. [Task 1]\n- Group benchmark recipient lists originate from Redis authorization snapshots or Feign `getSendAuthorizationSnapshot`; if that source is bypassed, load a fixed local member snapshot rather than merely removing authorization. [Task 1]\n- `locustfile_single.py` loads `users_*.json`, opens formal WebSockets, logs in with `cmd=1`, sends single chat with `cmd=5`, and keeps heartbeat/reconnect behavior. Run `locust -f locustfile_single.py --web-host 0.0.0.0 --web-port 8090`; a headless example is `locust -f locustfile_single.py --headless -u 500 -r 50 --run-time 10m --html result-500.html`. [Task 2]\n- Current script is not a strict capacity test: it selects among 100 ring targets with 40/40/20 activity waits and only observes sender response. Use fixed pairs, explicit send rate, pre-exported JSON data, receiver `cmd=27` accounting, and loss/duplicate/out-of-order metrics for comparable 500/800/1000/2000/5000-user runs. [Task 2]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- `BenchmarkMessagePath` measured only Netty plus an in-memory Channel because it bypassed `IMServiceImpl`; first lock down which layer is being measured, then implement a controlled branch in that layer. [Task 1]\n- Commenting a stranger-rate-limit step does not remove all external calls. Do not use `ss` alone as proof: instrument code-level counters/logs and obtain target-service evidence. Static review cannot establish P99 or capacity. [Task 1]\n- Treat `resp.success=false` as a Locust failure and verify receiver `cmd=27`; sender-only acknowledgements otherwise overstate delivery success. Do not embed credentials or query CRM/MySQL during the send window; prepare JSON beforehand. [Task 2]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM WebSocket EventLoop blocking audit\nscope: Read-only, source-backed review of whether IM WebSocket commands synchronously block the Netty EventLoop; use before planning performance remediation.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=the static call-chain finding is checkout-specific; recheck runtime instrumentation before quantifying latency or declaring production impact.\n\n## Task 1: Audit IM WebSocket EventLoop blocking chain\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-24T09-20-52-ucN3-im_websocket_eventloop_blocking_audit.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\24\\rollout-2026-07-24T17-20-52-019f936d-752b-7f81-8856-55d5b5dc7601.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-24T09:23:38+00:00, thread_id=019f936d-752b-7f81-8856-55d5b5dc7601, success: source review confirmed synchronous blocking paths; no code changed)\n\n### keywords\n\n- Netty, EventLoop, WebSocket, IMHandler, CommandDispatcher, ConversationServiceImpl, ConnectionManagerImpl, IMServiceImpl, Redisson, Feign, CompletableFuture.get(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS), CallerRunsPolicy\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user asked “目前代码的链路存在这个问题吗” and supplied a chain diagram -> give a definite, source-backed conclusion first; distinguish confirmed blocking from runtime-only impact. [Task 1]\n- when the request is an architecture/performance audit -> keep it read-only unless implementation is explicitly authorized; first locate and attribute the chain, then propose remediation separately. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- `CommandDispatcher.dispatch()` is called from `IMHandler.channelRead0()` and directly invokes login, chat, read-ack, revoke, reconnect, and call handlers; no business-executor handoff was found before these calls. [Task 1]\n- The login path synchronously does JWT validation, Redis route refresh, Redisson connection/cache work, DB conversation lookup, Feign user/group lookup, and offline-message DB read/delete plus Redis counter update. `ConversationServiceImpl.getRecentConversationList()` waits with `CompletableFuture.allOf(...).get(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS)` and reads Redis per conversation. [Task 1]\n- `ConnectionManagerImpl` uses synchronous Redisson bucket reads/writes; per-conversation cache updates add linear Redis round trips. Single/group send handlers directly invoke transactional `sendSingleMessage` / `sendGroupMessage`, including Redis, database, and in some modes synchronous Feign authorization. [Task 1]\n- `ModerationQueueConfig.groupInfoQueryExecutor` uses `CallerRunsPolicy`; saturation can run blocking Feign work on the submitting EventLoop. [Task 1]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Static review did not run a benchmark, slow-dependency injection, or EventLoop metrics; do not quantify production P99 impact from this evidence alone. [Task 1]\n- Do not async-wrap only one Feign call. Move the complete business command to a bounded business executor with fast rejection/degradation, avoid `CallerRunsPolicy` fallback to EventLoop, and add EventLoop pending-task, command-duration, dependency-P99, and rejection metrics. [Task 1]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM relation separation, Redis-only cutover, and warmup scheduling\nscope: Keep relations authoritative in CRM Account, plan a fail-closed Redis-only authorization cutover, and stagger repair warmups; the rollout is design/acceptance evidence, not production validation.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=recheck branch `dev-imtest`, Account/IM contracts, Redis state, and runtime topology; test/compile evidence does not replace middleware and real-client acceptance.\n\n## Task 1: Design and review friend/group relation separation implementation and acceptance plan\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-18T03-10-12-ETuk-im_relation_separation_redis_only_pressure_test_and_cron.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-07-18T11-10-17-019f7333-f282-7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T12:11:48+00:00, thread_id=019f7333-f282-7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4, success: design review passed; real-environment acceptance not run)\n\n### keywords\n\n- TB_FRIEND_RELATION, TB_GROUP_INFO, TB_GROUP_USER_RELATION, yopu-crm-account, SocialInternalFeignClient, fail-closed, groupMemberCheck, Outbox, P0/P1/P2\n\n## Task 2: Plan direct Redis-only authorization cutover\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-18T03-10-12-ETuk-im_relation_separation_redis_only_pressure_test_and_cron.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-07-18T11-10-17-019f7333-f282-7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T12:11:48+00:00, thread_id=019f7333-f282-7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4, success: direct cutover procedure designed)\n\n### keywords\n\n- yopu.im.auth.running-mode=redis_only, TB_RELATION_CACHE_INVALIDATION_OUTBOX, /user/internal/job/im-auth-warmup/users, failedCount=0, yopu:im:warmup:failed:*, feign rollback\n\n## Task 3: Stagger the five Redis warmup jobs\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-18T03-10-12-ETuk-im_relation_separation_redis_only_pressure_test_and_cron.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-07-18T11-10-17-019f7333-f282-7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T12:11:48+00:00, thread_id=019f7333-f282-7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4, success: warmup schedule designed)\n\n### keywords\n\n- Quartz CRON, 0 7/30 * * * ?, group-profiles, friend-views, group-member-views, after-commit, Outbox, skipped\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user requested “可落地的实施测试验收方案 md，然后评审，评审不过的话需要修改，直到评审通过” -> verify current code facts first, then provide boundaries, P0/P1/P2 tests, release gates, rollback, and iterative review. [Task 1]\n- for this relation plan, “保留公开接口、不迁移数据、不新建关系微服务” -> keep the minimal-risk CRM internal-domain boundary. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- `yopu-crm-account` is authoritative for `TB_FRIEND_RELATION`, `TB_GROUP_INFO`, and `TB_GROUP_USER_RELATION`; IM reads the minimum relation data through internal Feign and must not write relation tables, duplicate relation data, migrate data, or change public `/user/social/**` APIs. Authorization is fail-closed; on group dissolution, clear every `groupMemberCheck(userId:groupId)`, not only the member-list cache. [Task 1]\n- Even when bypassing SHADOW, deploy Account and relation/Outbox DDL, validate Outbox, run all five warmups and samples (`skipped=false`, `failedCount=0`, `yopu:im:warmup:failed:*` empty), then switch every IM node to `yopu.im.auth.running-mode=redis_only`. Roll back only to `feign` with a rolling IM restart; retain Redis, Outbox, and DDL. [Task 2]\n- Stagger the five repair jobs every 30 minutes: users `0 7/30 * * * ?`, groups `0 11/30 * * * ?`, group profiles `0 15/30 * * * ?`, friend views `0 19/30 * * * ?`, and group-member views `0 23/30 * * * ?`. Correctness comes from after-commit + Outbox; warmup is only repair/coverage scanning. If jobs overrun or often skip, investigate duration, failed sets, and MySQL/Redis load before moving to hourly staggering. [Task 3]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Markdown trailing double spaces break `git diff --check`; PowerShell Chinese-path/PPT handling needs `Path.glob('*.pptx')`, `PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8`, and `$doc = '...'` (not `a='...'`). Static review and documentation cannot replace Redis, RabbitMQ, Nacos, dual-node, and real-App acceptance. [Task 1]\n- Do not enable `redis_only` before warmup/sample evidence: a missing snapshot must deny authorization, not silently fall back to Feign. Do not shorten an overrunning warmup cycle; diagnose load first. [Task 2][Task 3]\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM offline delivery, JPush environment isolation, and horizontal-scale safety\nscope: Audit, refactor, validate, and deploy Yopu IM online/offline delivery, JPush, RabbitMQ, DB migration, and Dev/production push isolation.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=use for this checkout's yopu-im architecture; production claims require live Nacos, RabbitMQ, DB, and client verification.\n\n## Task 1: Audit IM offline delivery, add a business-level offline-Push switch, and assess Dev/production JPush isolation\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-16T06-33-52-OCWh-im_offline_push_jpush_environment_isolation.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\16\\rollout-2026-07-16T14-33-54-019f69a1-b1d8-7a71-9ee3-ffa18e849f35.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-01T02:50:13+00:00, thread_id=019f69a1-b1d8-7a71-9ee3-ffa18e849f35, git_branch=dev-imtest, success: code audit and focused tests; live Nacos/device isolation remains unverified)\n\n### keywords\n\n- offline-push, JPush, push.jiguang.enabled, im.offline-push.enabled, im.offline-push.cleanup-enabled, Registration ID, AppKey, Nacos, Redis, RabbitMQ, WebSocket, heartbeat, OfflinePushDispatcher, OfflinePushTaskAdmissionService, 1011\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user challenged the meaning of `push.jiguang.enabled: false` -> inspect the exact code path controlled by the existing configuration before proposing another switch. [Task 1]\n- when the user requested a business-level total switch and asked whether switches should be merged -> preserve distinct business, provider, and cleanup responsibilities rather than conflating them. [Task 1]\n- when the user asked to leave unrelated workspace changes untouched -> restrict edits to the named OfflinePush properties, admission, dispatcher, config, and tests. [Task 1]\n- when assessing whether a Dev package can receive production Push -> verify runtime Nacos namespace/config, client AppKey/package name, binding endpoint, and Redis isolation; source YAML alone is insufficient. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- `IMServiceImpl.deliverMessageToUser()` checks active local Netty channels, Redis multi-client routes, then remote MQ before offline persistence. Offline Push is separate: admission/persistence -> `OfflinePushDispatcher` -> direct/group RabbitMQ queues -> `OfflinePushTaskConsumer` -> `triggerOfflinePush()` -> `PushService`. [Task 1]\n- `push.jiguang.enabled` controls JPush SDK/provider bean creation via `PushAutoConfiguration`; it blocks JPush calls but does not itself stop offline-message persistence or task creation. `im.offline-push.enabled` is the business switch: it blocks new task admission and real-time MQ dispatch, and makes claimed old tasks `SKIPPED` without calling JPush. Normal WebSocket delivery and offline-message persistence remain enabled. [Task 1]\n- Keep `push.jiguang.enabled` as provider-level safety control and `im.offline-push.cleanup-enabled` as historical-task cleanup control; do not merge them into one ambiguous switch. [Task 1]\n- Device bindings are Redis keys `push:device:user:{userId}` and `push:device:reg:{registrationId}` with a 90-day TTL. An accepted JPush API request is not device delivery; use delivery acknowledgement, device logs, and `msg_id + registration_id` to verify. `1011` means no valid Push target; a single-device request can clean its invalid binding, but bulk requests cannot identify it precisely. [Task 1]\n- Different dev/prod source AppKey fingerprints reduce accidental cross-delivery, but Nacos can override runtime configuration. A real cross-environment proof requires uninstall-prod -> install-dev -> bind/login -> send from production, plus Nacos, AppKey/package, binding endpoint, and Redis checks. [Task 1]\n- For Pre cleanup, remove both the `push:device:user:{userId}` Hash field and matching `push:device:reg:{registrationId}` reverse key; a full cleanup must use batched Redis `SCAN`, never `KEYS`, after Pre offline Push is disabled. [Task 1]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Do not stop `im-core` or ordinary message MQ consumers to disable offline Push; that can aff